# Project governance

- Read AGENTS.md before planning or modifying files.
- Work on one approved milestone or task at a time.
- Do not generate speculative modules for future features.
- Prefer functions and small cohesive modules over class hierarchies.
- Do not create interfaces with only one implementation unless a real boundary requires it.
- Do not create wrapper functions that add no validation, transformation or behavior.
- Do not duplicate contracts or business rules.
- Keep HTTP routes thin and domain logic independent from web frameworks.
- Do not modify unrelated files.
- Do not install or upgrade dependencies without explicit approval.
- Do not claim completion until relevant checks have been executed.
